# Baseline security headers (Phase 1 cold audit #35) + Wave 2 hardening (#38): CSP now ENFORCED
# (2026-09-03) after a report-only cycle. The allowlist was validated against the live report-only
# console: every code-referenced origin (clerk.traxwax.com, cloud.umami.is, cdn.jsdelivr.net, fonts,
# supabase, img.clerk.com/Discogs CDN via img-src https:) plus these RUNTIME origins the console/Clerk
# env surfaced — static.cloudflareinsights.com (Cloudflare Pages auto-injects its Web Analytics beacon
# SCRIPT; its beacon POST is same-origin /cdn-cgi/rum so needs no connect entry); gateway.umami.is
# (umami LOADS from cloud.umami.is but SENDS events to gateway.umami.is — connect-src); and Cloudflare
# Turnstile — challenges.cloudflare.com — because Clerk bot-protection IS enabled on the production
# instance (captchaProvider=turnstile, signUpCaptcha=true), so the "smart" widget loads a SCRIPT +
# FRAME + posts on sign-up/sign-in; clerk-telemetry.com (Clerk telemetry POST, harmless) is allowed to
# keep the enforced console clean. 'unsafe-inline' stays for script/style (the app is inline-style heavy
# + a few inline guard scripts); tighten to hashes/nonces later. SRI intentionally omitted — Clerk @6 /
# supabase-js @2 / umami script.js are moving version tags where a pinned hash breaks on update; the
# script-src allowlist is the supply-chain mitigation instead. ROLLBACK: if sign-in ever breaks, rename
# the header back to Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only (unblocks everything, keeps reporting).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://clerk.traxwax.com https://cloud.umami.is https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://sfipqknrbvamwwahwxnl.supabase.co https://clerk.traxwax.com https://cloud.umami.is https://gateway.umami.is https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://clerk-telemetry.com; frame-src 'self' https://clerk.traxwax.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; form-action 'self' https://clerk.traxwax.com
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()

# Issue #9: fixed asset names (/app.js, /boot.js, HTML shells) served stale from browser
# cache across deploys — observed at launch as a pre-launch app.js dead-ending on
# "Couldn't load collection.json" while production served correct code. no-cache means
# "revalidate before every use": Pages serves ETags, so an unchanged file is a cheap 304
# and a deploy is picked up on the next load. HTML + entry-point JS/CSS only.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/app
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/app/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/app/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/collection.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/app.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/dna.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/boot.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/boot.ui.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/boot.clerk.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/styles.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/account
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/account/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# The baked per-release files are write-once immutable (Stage C enriches the DB, not
# these) — a week of browser cache is safe and spares the modal's fallback tier a fetch.
/releases/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
